# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host state out of
# the image: server_data/ and backups/ hold the live database, the encrypted
# document blobs and the master key. Baking those into a published image
# would leak them to anyone who can pull it.
server_data/
backups/
.venv/
venv/

.git/
.github/
.claude-notes/

**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documentation and one-off dev scripts: not needed at runtime, and excluding
# them means a README edit doesn't invalidate the Docker layer cache.
*.md
client/verify-phase*.mjs
server/scripts_phase5_live_server.py
create-user.ps1
